{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And he cried out.</b> This tree — we do not know what it was; it was a wondrous thing. And if the waters had been still, we would say it was by way of medicine. And what the Sages said is correct:" "<b>There He set for him.</b> For Israel." "Statute and ordinance, to discipline them and to teach them." "And the sense of \"and there He tested him\": in the manner of \"for YHWH your Elohim is testing you, to know whether you love Him\" (Deuteronomy 13:4), and likewise \"He afflicted you and let you go hungry\" (ibid. 8:3) and \"and to test you, to do you good in your end\" (ibid. 8:16) — to do good to those who endured, in that they did not complain against Moses."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:54.579941275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}